WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.844 --> 00:00:04.919
On line 3 too-light cartons keep coming out of the filling unit.

2
00:00:05.992 --> 00:00:10.230
The module Measurement and SPC in depth goes beyond the basics.

3
00:00:10.936 --> 00:00:13.107
You read the fill weight with statistics.

4
00:00:14.134 --> 00:00:15.341
You are the engineer.

5
00:00:16.053 --> 00:00:19.315
After the shift you and the team lead follow the fill weight.

6
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.193
First the measuring itself and what the process does,

7
00:00:23.344 --> 00:00:26.200
with measurement systems and with control charts.

8
00:00:27.248 --> 00:00:29.767
Then what the process can do and how you hold it,

9
00:00:29.907 --> 00:00:32.740
with capability and SPC on the shop floor.

10
00:00:34.051 --> 00:00:36.431
The first topic is Measurement systems.

11
00:00:37.151 --> 00:00:40.355
Every reading is the true value plus a measurement error.

12
00:00:41.385 --> 00:00:43.893
You weigh the cartons at the end of the belt.

13
00:00:44.666 --> 00:00:47.789
A noisy scale makes the spread look larger than it is.

14
00:00:48.832 --> 00:00:51.317
You study the weighing with a gauge R and R.

15
00:00:52.044 --> 00:00:54.749
Two people weigh the same carton a few times.

16
00:00:56.069 --> 00:00:58.391
The second topic is Control charts.

17
00:00:59.105 --> 00:01:01.822
A control chart plots a result over time.

18
00:01:02.776 --> 00:01:06.990
The centre line and two limits show what line 3 does by itself.

19
00:01:08.039 --> 00:01:11.801
A point outside a limit is a signal to look for what has changed.

20
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.101
You weigh equal batches and count the too-light cartons.

21
00:01:16.824 --> 00:01:19.158
You plot that count on an np chart.

22
00:01:20.529 --> 00:01:22.468
The third topic is Capability.

23
00:01:23.151 --> 00:01:26.379
It compares the spread of weighed values with the tolerance.

24
00:01:27.372 --> 00:01:30.925
First you make the process stable, then you measure capability.

25
00:01:31.915 --> 00:01:34.980
You read that in a capability report from the software.

26
00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.103
The fourth topic is SPC on the shop floor.

27
00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.780
There SPC is a routine.

28
00:01:42.798 --> 00:01:47.779
Measure more often where things change, such as after a changeover of line 3.

29
00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:51.979
You do a first-off check and weigh one carton first.

30
00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:57.609
That is how you and the team lead follow the fill weight with data, not by feel.

31
00:01:58.902 --> 00:01:59.703
The whole map.

32
00:02:00.448 --> 00:02:05.568
The second station is Measurement and SPC in depth, in Making the plant better.

33
00:02:06.596 --> 00:02:08.790
Each of the four topics has four levels.

34
00:02:09.857 --> 00:02:12.272
Start at Basics level with measurement error.

35
00:02:13.008 --> 00:02:15.748
Every number you use later comes from a reading.

36
00:02:16.774 --> 00:02:21.024
At Working knowledge level come gauge studies, the right control chart,

37
00:02:21.163 --> 00:02:24.205
Cpk versus Ppk and over-adjustment.

38
00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:27.836
At Advanced level come visual inspection,

39
00:02:27.928 --> 00:02:31.341
small shifts, non-normal data and reading patterns.

40
00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.959
At Expert level come destructive tests,

41
00:02:35.145 --> 00:02:39.046
short runs, capability requirements and an SPC programme.
